WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.600
One of the problems in health care

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.900
is that we have broken cultures
in health care.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.600
And that senior doctors

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.120
or especially hospital administrators

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.600
don't know what their job is.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.000
When you ask them,
"What's your priority?"

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.100
They say "patients."

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.100
No, it's not.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:21.700
It's to take care of the people
who work in the hospital.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.600
You take care of the people 
who take care of the people.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:25.800
That's what you do.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:29.340
Every administrator and every senior doctor
and senior nurse

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:31.900
should be preoccupied with one thing
and one thing only:

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.200
are my doctors OK, are my nurses OK,
is my staff OK?

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.100
And if you get that right

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.000
they will devote all of their time and energy

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.000
to taking care of each other and the patients.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.900
The problem is we have cultures

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.100
in which they think money is more important

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:47.200
or patients are more important

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:50.000
or anything else other than the doctors,
the nurses and the staff.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.000
And so the doctors, the nurses and staff 
are forced every day

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.100
to spend time and energy to protect themselves

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.800
from their own leaders

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:58.500
and take energy away

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.400
from doing the right thing for the patients.

00:01:04.315 --> 00:01:05.315
 

00:01:05.925 --> 00:01:07.375
 

00:01:08.015 --> 00:01:09.015
 

